From b82396db3e5cd2c544fe83fedc52b820d9c16807 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoXider <neoxider@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 13:27:53 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] cq: packed f16d4 KV type (12 bits/value), GQA-grouped FA
 vector kernel, lazily mapped KV buffer, VRAM report

- GGML_TYPE_F16D4 = 60: F16 with the 4 low mantissa bits dropped, block of 32 = 48 bytes (hi byte plane + nibble plane)
- CUDA: set_rows quantizer, to_fp16/fp32 converters (prefill via f16 scratch), fused decode in the FA vector kernel
  (8 values per thread: 2 loads, 2 ALU ops, 4 byte permutes)
- flash_attn_ext_vec_gqa: single-token decode kernel that serves all query heads of a GQA group from one K/V read
  (default for f16d4; env CQ_FA_VEC_GQA=1 also for f16/q8_0/q4_0, =0 off)
- CQ_KV_LAZY=1: KV cache in a CUDA VMM buffer that maps physical memory for rows [0, n_kv) on demand
- CQ_VRAM_REPORT=1: per-process DXGI local video memory after every llama_decode (Windows)
